\begin{itemize}
\item closure of the Lie algebra under recursion-induced commutators,
\item existence of non-trivial, anomaly-free fermion representations,
\item compatibility with curvature coupling $\alpha R_{\text{geom}}R_{\text{rec}}$.
\end{itemize}
Larger groups (e.g.\ $SU(5)$, $SO(10)$) introduce additional generators
that couple to $R_{\text{rec}}$ in a way that breaks boundedness or
anomaly cancellation. Smaller groups fail to accommodate observed
fermion content. The unique solution satisfying all constraints is
$SU(3)\times SU(2)\times U(1)$.
\end{proof}

\section{Anomaly Cancellation}

